From 8797543cb931c408fa8b8bd2ba8aa063d0489a3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 22:45:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bound a relevance search's match set: the newest-N cut, as
 query parameters
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A NIP-50 search for a common word costs seconds on the production relay
(`bitcoin` 4.4s, `nostr` and `the` 16s on 2026-09-03, at limit 1 and limit
200 alike) because the relevance profile matches and scores every posting the
word touches; benchmark/README.md §5 said the only thing that beats that stops
being exact, and the relay has now asked for a 200ms page. So the first option
on that list is taken, on the terms it was excluded for: the answer changes,
and the change is measured (§6).

EventYql.build sends `ranking.matchPhase.attribute=created_at`, descending,
`maxHits=VESPA_SEARCH_MATCH_PHASE_MAX_HITS` (default 10,000) on the relevance
profiles — search, text, rank_desc, rank_asc, sort_followers — and on nothing
else: not the keyed lookups the expansion makes, not plain recall or the
recency pair (whose schema-side cut this client mirrors), and never a COUNT,
whose totalCount a capped match phase would cap. VespaEventIndex.searchRoot
accepts the match-phase degradation on a query that asked for it, and
recallRoot widens a SHORT cut page ten-fold once before running exact, so a
sparse lens cannot end a pager early. No schema change: under the depth every
page and every count is byte-identical, and `…=0` is the old store.

Measured on 1.31M real staging events with the observer's real lens (README
§6): where the cut engages the cost is the cut rather than the corpus (`the`
331ms uncut, 69ms at 10,000; the same cut is what `sort:recent` already rides
at 0.5s on production against 19s uncut), and the page becomes the
best-ranked of the newest N — 0-5 of the exact top-10 survive for `the`,
`nostr`, `bitcoin` at cuts that engaged. Stated in the constant's KDoc so the
number is read as the trade it is.

MockVespaEngine cuts a relevance search that asks for it (below a depth a
test sets) and logs every search's parameters, which is how the ladder —
cut, widened, exact — is pinned by VespaEventIndexTest.

