+### 6. What was taken after all: the newest-N cut (2026-09-03)
+
+The relay asked for a 200ms page, and section 5 is right that no exact answer
+gets there: the floor is the posting walk, and `nostr` is 14.5s of it at one
+thread. So the first option in that list is now taken, on the terms it was
+excluded for — **it changes the answer, and the change is measured**.
+
+`EventYql.build` sends `ranking.matchPhase.attribute=created_at`, descending,
+`maxHits=VESPA_SEARCH_MATCH_PHASE_MAX_HITS` (default 10,000) as QUERY
+PARAMETERS on the relevance profiles — `search`, `text`, `rank_desc`,
+`rank_asc`, `sort_followers` — and on nothing else: not the keyed lookups
+(the expansion's, whose match set the query named itself), not plain recall or
+the recency pair (their own schema-side cut, whose per-node depth this client
+mirrors), and never a COUNT (a capped match phase caps `totalCount`, the trap
+`countProfileOf` already documents). `VespaEventIndex.searchRoot` accepts the
+match-phase degradation on a query that asked for it, and `recallRoot` widens
+a SHORT cut page ten-fold once before running exact, so a sparse lens never
+ends a pager early. No schema change: the same profiles keep serving exact
+answers wherever the cut does not engage, and `…=0` is the old store.
+
+Measured on **1.31M real staging events** captured read-only on 2026-09-03 —
+1.19M kind 1 (the newest ~35 days), 100k kind 0, all 367 kind-10040s and the
+provider `7d7ffd72…`'s 30382 cards for every author in the slice (11.2k cards
+for 190k distinct authors; the trust gate deletes the other 94%). The store's
+own YQL (`searchTrace`, `SEARCH_YQL=1`), re-sent with the cut as parameters;
+`min_rank 2`, kind 1, limit 40, 4 match threads, p50 of 5 by Vespa's own
+`searchtime`; the cut page's top-40 compared with the exact page's:
+
+| word | uncut | served | cut 2,000 | 5,000 | 10,000 | 20,000 | 50,000 |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| `the` | 331 ms | 30.5k | 36 ms · 0/10 | 50 ms · 0/10 | 69 ms · 0/10 | 165 ms · 2/10 | 319 ms · exact |
+| `nostr` | 186 ms | 23.8k | 88 ms · 1/10 | 91 ms · 4/10 | 127 ms · 5/10 | 234 ms · exact | 205 ms · exact |
+| `bitcoin` | 145 ms | 6.9k | 42 ms · 1/10 | 83 ms · 2/10 | 71 ms · exact | 94 ms · exact | 134 ms · exact |
+| `bitc` | 85 ms | 7.2k | 36 ms · 2/10 | 52 ms · 3/10 | exact | exact | exact |
+| `love` | 118 ms | 1.7k | 70 ms · 5/10 | exact | exact | exact | exact |
+| `lightning` | 55 ms | 861 | exact | exact | exact | exact | exact |
+| `zap` | 35 ms | 1.2k | exact | exact | exact | exact | exact |
+
+("served" is the uncut `totalCount`, net of the gate; "n/10" how many of the
+exact top-10 the cut page keeps; "exact" — the cut did not engage, count and
+page byte-identical, `degraded` false. One thread: `the` uncut 629ms, at
+10,000 53ms; `nostr` 423 / 227ms — the threads help the uncut shape and not
+the cut one.)
+
+- **The cost is the cut, not the corpus.** Behind a cut of N is the newest
+  window holding N matches, walked against every matcher — N over the word's
+  selectivity, whatever the corpus. The same cut on the production corpus is
+  what `sort:recent` already rides: 0.46-0.50s there at one thread WITH the
+  relay's floor (section 1), against 4.9-19.2s uncut.
+- **Where it does not engage, nothing changes.** Under the depth every page
+  and every count is byte-identical. Only words in a few percent of the corpus
+  are cut, and those are exactly the words that cost seconds.
+- **Where it engages, the page is a different page** — the best-ranked of the
+  newest N, not of the corpus. The trust-ranked top-10 for `the` or `nostr` is
+  spread across the month and the newest few thousand matches hold 0-5 of it.
+  That is the trade `sort:recent` already makes, made the default for the one
+  shape nothing else can bound, and stated in the constant's KDoc so nobody
+  reads a 69ms `the` as a free lunch.
+
+The harness that produced the table is a plain-node script over `/search/`
+(the store's YQL plus `ranking.matchPhase.*`), kept with the relay-side
+write-up (`vespa-relay` `docs/search-latency.md`); `searchTrace` prints the
+YQL it needs.
+
